#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:9
msgid "Decide how to internationalize the Slidev deck (JA/EN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:11
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:13
msgid ""
"The PyCon JP 2026 talk deck (`slides/slides.md`, selected in "
"[ADR-0001](0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md)) currently "
"mixes Japanese and English inline within each slide. For example, the "
"cover slide shows both \"Server-less 3D Visualization\" and "
"\"サーバーレス3D可視化の実現\" side by side, and the speaker panel renders both "
"\"Tetsuo Koyama\" and \"小山 哲央\" together. This couples the two language "
"versions: editing one language requires touching the same Markdown block "
"as the other, and there is no clean way to present a single-language view"
" of the talk. Issue [#361](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-"
"wasm/issues/361) captures the user-facing need to internationalize the "
"deck (JA/EN) with a way to switch between languages, and "
"[#333](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/333) proposes "
"adopting [`slidev-addon-i18nb`](https://github.com/LarchLiu/slidev-addon-"
"i18n) as one implementation approach. Which i18n strategy should we adopt"
" for the Slidev deck?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:15
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:17
msgid ""
"**Single-language rendering**: A viewer must be able to see the entire "
"deck rendered in one language (JA or EN) at a time, without the other "
"language cluttering the slide. This is a knock-out criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:18
msgid ""
"**Independent maintenance of JA/EN content**: Editing one language's text"
" must not require touching the other language's content, so the two "
"versions can be maintained independently and reviewed separately in PRs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:19
msgid ""
"**Compatibility with the existing deployment pipeline**: The i18n "
"solution must work with the deployment strategy established in "
"[ADR-0002](0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md) — GitHub"
" Pages (Deploy from branch) with `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages` for main "
"and `rossjrw/pr-preview-action` for per-PR previews, both building via "
"`slidev build`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:20
msgid ""
"**Zero-cost / GitHub-native tooling**: The project is an open-source, "
"community-driven effort; the i18n solution must not require paid "
"services, external API keys, or accounts beyond what is already in the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:21
msgid ""
"**Authoring ergonomics**: The bilingual content should be authorable "
"efficiently with hot-reload preview, so iteration is fast before the "
"talk. Slide structure (layout, components, code blocks) should remain "
"easy to write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:22
msgid ""
"**Build-time impact**: The i18n solution should not significantly "
"increase build time or bundle size, since the deck is built in CI on "
"every PR and on push to main."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:24
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:26
msgid ""
"[`slidev-addon-i18nb`](https://github.com/LarchLiu/slidev-addon-i18n) — "
"Slidev addon built on Vue i18n; provides a per-language translation layer"
" with a runtime language switcher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:27
msgid ""
"Two separate decks (`slides.ja.md` / `slides.en.md`) — full language "
"separation; each deck is built and deployed independently"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:28
msgid ""
"Keep the current inline JA/EN approach — both languages on every slide; "
"no i18n tooling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:29
msgid ""
"Custom Vue i18n integration — manually integrate [`vue-"
"i18n`](https://github.com/intlify/vue-i18n) with a custom language-"
"switcher component, without the Slidev addon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:30
msgid ""
"Build-time locale switching — single `slides.md` with conditional content"
" blocks, built twice with a locale environment variable, producing two "
"static deployments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:32
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:34
msgid ""
"Chosen option: \"slidev-addon-i18nb\", because it is the only option that"
" satisfies every decision driver simultaneously — it provides runtime "
"single-language rendering with an in-deck language switcher, stores "
"translations in separate YAML files so JA/EN content is maintained "
"independently, integrates with the existing `slidev build` pipeline "
"without deployment changes, requires no paid services or API keys in "
"manual-translation mode, and keeps the slide structure in a single "
"`slides.md` file so layout and code blocks are authored once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:36
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:38
msgid ""
"Good, because a viewer can switch between JA and EN at runtime via a "
"language-switcher control in the Slidev navigation, seeing the entire "
"deck in a single language without the other language on screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:39
msgid ""
"Good, because translations live in separate YAML files (`locales/ja.yml`,"
" `locales/en.yml`), so editing one language does not require touching the"
" other or the slide structure file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:40
msgid ""
"Good, because the slide structure (layouts, Vue components, code blocks, "
"iframes) is authored once in `slides.md` with `{{ $t(\"key\") }}` "
"placeholders, avoiding the duplication and drift risk of two separate "
"decks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:41
msgid ""
"Good, because the addon is a standard Slidev addon registered in "
"headmatter, so `slidev build` and the existing CI workflows in `deploy-"
"slides.yml` and `preview-slides.yml` continue to work without structural "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:42
msgid ""
"Good, because the manual-translation mode requires no API keys or "
"external services, satisfying the zero-cost / GitHub-native driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:43
msgid ""
"Bad, because every text string in the current `slides.md` must be "
"extracted into translation keys and replaced with `{{ $t(\"key\") }}` "
"calls, which is a significant one-time migration effort for a 23-slide "
"deck with complex HTML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:44
msgid ""
"Bad, because the addon has a very small community (2 GitHub stars, v0.2.6"
" as of 2026-08-01), so there is a risk of the project becoming "
"unmaintained; we accept this risk because the addon is MIT-licensed and "
"thin enough to fork or replace if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:45
msgid ""
"Bad, because the `{{ $t(\"key\") }}` syntax does not work inside HTML "
"attributes or `<script setup>` blocks without additional handling, so "
"some slides with complex inline HTML may need refactoring or custom Vue "
"components for their translated text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:46
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the addon's AI auto-transform feature (which uses a "
"Gemini API key) is available but optional; we will use manual translation"
" to stay zero-cost and GitHub-native."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:48
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:50
msgid "Compliance with this decision will be confirmed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:52
msgid ""
"`slidev-addon-i18nb` is listed in the `addons` frontmatter of "
"`slides/slides.md` and in `slides/package.json` dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:53
msgid ""
"A `locales/` directory exists under `slides/` containing `ja.yml` and "
"`en.yml` with translation keys for all user-facing text in the deck."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:54
msgid ""
"`slides/slides.md` uses `{{ $t(\"key\") }}` placeholders for translatable"
" text, with no inline JA/EN mixing on any slide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:55
msgid ""
"Running `slidev dev` locally and switching the language via the addon's "
"language-switcher control renders the entire deck in the selected "
"language (JA or EN)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:56
msgid ""
"`slidev build --base /pyvista-wasm/slides/` succeeds and the built deck "
"is deployed to GitHub Pages at `https://tkoyama010.github.io/pyvista-"
"wasm/slides/` with the language switcher functional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:57
msgid ""
"A per-PR preview built via `preview-slides.yml` renders correctly in both"
" languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:58
msgid ""
"All existing slide content (23 slides) is migrated to the i18n structure "
"without loss of material — verified by comparing the rendered output "
"against the pre-migration deck."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:60
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:62
msgid ""
"slidev-addon-i18nb — Slidev addon built on Vue i18n with a runtime "
"language switcher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:64
msgid ""
"See [https://github.com/LarchLiu/slidev-addon-"
"i18n](https://github.com/LarchLiu/slidev-addon-i18n)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:66
msgid ""
"Good, because it provides a runtime language switcher in the Slidev "
"navigation bar, so a viewer can toggle between JA and EN without leaving "
"the deck — fully satisfying the single-language-rendering driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:67
msgid ""
"Good, because translations are stored in separate YAML files "
"(`locales/ja.yml`, `locales/en.yml`), so editing one language does not "
"require touching the other — fully satisfying the independent-maintenance"
" driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:68
msgid ""
"Good, because the slide structure (layouts, components, code blocks) is "
"authored once in `slides.md` with `{{ $t(\"key\") }}` placeholders, "
"avoiding the duplication and drift risk of two separate decks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:69
msgid ""
"Good, because it is a standard Slidev addon registered via headmatter "
"`addons:` — no build pipeline changes are needed; `slidev build` "
"continues to produce a single SPA deployment, satisfying compatibility "
"with ADR-0002."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:70
msgid ""
"Good, because the manual-translation mode requires no API keys, external "
"accounts, or paid services — satisfying the zero-cost / GitHub-native "
"driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:71
msgid ""
"Good, because it is built on [vue-i18n](https://github.com/intlify/vue-"
"i18n), a widely adopted i18n library for Vue, so the translation "
"mechanism is well-understood."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:72
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the addon's AI auto-transform feature can accelerate the"
" initial translation extraction, but it requires a Gemini API key and is "
"therefore optional rather than a core workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:73
msgid ""
"Bad, because the addon has a very small community (2 GitHub stars, 0 "
"forks, v0.2.6 as of 2026-08-01), so there is a maintenance-risk if the "
"upstream project becomes inactive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:74
msgid ""
"Bad, because migrating the existing 23-slide deck requires extracting "
"every text string into translation keys and replacing it with `{{ "
"$t(\"key\") }}` — a significant one-time effort, especially for slides "
"with complex inline HTML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:75
msgid ""
"Bad, because `{{ $t(\"key\") }}` works in Markdown text and Vue template "
"interpolations but not in raw HTML attributes or `<script setup>` logic "
"without additional workarounds, so some slides may need refactoring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:77
msgid ""
"Two separate decks (slides.ja.md / slides.en.md) — full language "
"separation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:79
msgid ""
"Good, because each deck is a complete, clean single-language file — no "
"i18n tooling, no translation keys, no `$t()` syntax; authoring stays "
"plain Markdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:80
msgid ""
"Good, because it is trivially compatible with the existing deployment "
"pipeline: build each deck separately with `slidev build` and deploy to "
"different subpaths (e.g. `/slides/ja/` and `/slides/en/`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:81
msgid ""
"Good, because it is zero-cost and GitHub-native with no external "
"dependencies beyond what Slidev already provides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:82
msgid ""
"Good, because each language can be reviewed independently in a PR — a JA "
"text fix touches only `slides.ja.md`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:83
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the existing `slides/slides.md` can be split into two "
"files mechanically, though the effort is comparable to the addon "
"migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:84
msgid ""
"Bad, because the slide structure (layouts, components, code blocks, "
"iframes) is duplicated across two files, so structural changes must be "
"applied twice — doubling the maintenance burden and creating drift risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:85
msgid ""
"Bad, because there is no in-deck language switcher; a viewer must "
"navigate to a different URL to switch languages, which is less seamless "
"than a runtime toggle and may not fully satisfy the \"switch the "
"presentation language\" acceptance criterion in "
"[#361](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/361)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:86
msgid ""
"Bad, because the CI workflows (`deploy-slides.yml`, `preview-slides.yml`)"
" must be modified to build and deploy two decks instead of one, adding "
"build-time and workflow complexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:88
msgid "Keep the current inline JA/EN approach — both languages on every slide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:90
msgid ""
"Good, because it requires zero migration effort — the deck already works "
"this way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:91
msgid ""
"Good, because it requires no additional tooling, dependencies, or build "
"pipeline changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:92
msgid ""
"Good, because a single `slides.md` file and a single build produce the "
"deployed deck, keeping the pipeline simple."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:93
msgid ""
"Neutral, because both languages are always visible to the audience, which"
" may be acceptable for a bilingual conference like PyCon JP but does not "
"meet the user story in [#361](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-"
"wasm/issues/361)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:94
msgid ""
"Bad, because the two language versions are coupled — editing a JA string "
"requires touching the same Markdown block as the EN string, failing the "
"independent-maintenance driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:95
msgid ""
"Bad, because there is no single-language view; every slide shows both JA "
"and EN simultaneously, failing the single-language-rendering knock-out "
"criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:96
msgid ""
"Bad, because slides become visually cluttered with two languages on "
"screen, reducing readability and presentation quality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:98
msgid ""
"Custom Vue i18n integration — manually integrate vue-i18n without the "
"Slidev addon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:100
msgid ""
"See [https://github.com/intlify/vue-i18n](https://github.com/intlify/vue-"
"i18n)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:102
msgid ""
"Good, because it uses vue-i18n directly — a mature, widely adopted "
"library (~3.5k GitHub stars) with extensive documentation and community "
"support, avoiding the small-community risk of slidev-addon-i18nb."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:103
msgid ""
"Good, like the addon, it provides runtime language switching and separate"
" translation files, satisfying the single-language-rendering and "
"independent-maintenance drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:104
msgid ""
"Good, because it is zero-cost and requires no external API keys or "
"accounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:105
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the translation YAML files and `{{ $t(\"key\") }}` "
"syntax are the same as with the addon, so the migration effort for the "
"slide content is identical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:106
msgid ""
"Bad, because it requires manually writing the Slidev integration layer — "
"a custom language-switcher Vue component, a custom nav-controls override,"
" and the vue-i18n plugin setup — duplicating what slidev-addon-i18nb "
"already provides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:107
msgid ""
"Bad, because the custom integration is additional code to maintain and "
"test, increasing the project's surface area for a one-time talk deck."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:108
msgid ""
"Bad, because there is no Slidev-specific documentation for manually "
"integrating vue-i18n, so the setup requires trial-and-error and is harder"
" to review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:110
msgid ""
"Build-time locale switching — single source, built twice with a locale "
"environment variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:112
msgid ""
"Good, because it keeps a single `slides.md` source file, avoiding the "
"duplication and drift risk of two separate decks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:113
msgid ""
"Good, because it is zero-cost and GitHub-native — no external "
"dependencies beyond Slidev itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:114
msgid ""
"Good, because each build produces a clean single-language deck, "
"satisfying the single-language-rendering driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:115
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the conditional content blocks (e.g., `<div "
"v-if=\"$locale === 'ja'\">...</div>`) are straightforward to write but "
"interleave both languages in the same file, partially coupling them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:116
msgid ""
"Bad, because there is no runtime language switcher — the viewer must "
"navigate to a different URL to switch languages, less seamless than a "
"runtime toggle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:117
msgid ""
"Bad, because the CI workflows must build the deck twice (once per locale)"
" and deploy to separate subpaths, doubling build time and adding workflow"
" complexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:118
msgid ""
"Bad, because interleaving JA and EN content in the same Markdown block "
"(even with `v-if`) means a text edit in one language touches the same "
"block as the other, partially failing the independent-maintenance driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md:120
msgid "More Information"
msgstr ""

